      "location": "Proof step 1.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "It asserts for “any t” that ||x(t)-x(t_*)|| <= integral from t_* to t of ||V(x(s))|| ds. The cited norm-integral theorem expressly requires lower limit <= upper limit and says the displayed inequality is false with reversed limits. For V=1, x(t)=t, and t<t_*, this asserts |t-t_*| <= t-t_*, which is false.",
