      "id": "lem-linear-matrix-odes-have-unique-global-solutions-on-a-given-interval",
      "location": "Proof step 2.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "For all t in J it writes ||Y(t)|| <= ||Y_0|| + M integral from t_0 to t of ||Y(s)|| ds, then invokes Gronwall. The cited Gronwall theorem requires t_0 <= t; its reflected version instead uses integral from t to t_0. The displayed estimate is false on the left: for n=1, C=-1, Y_0=1, t_0=0, t=-1, its right side is 2-e while ||Y(-1)||=e.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "7edf23d793c794e73265a7d7bf485db0b3655aa63cda19bc6d95789556b30025"
    },
    {
