      "id": "thm-c1-dependence-of-solutions-on-initial-data",
      "location": "Proof step 4.1",
      "defect": "unlicensed-inference",
      "evidence": "Step 3.1 establishes difference-quotient convergence only for a fixed y and direction h. Step 4.1 says “Therefore the directional derivatives assemble into the matrix solution D_y Phi,” but no uniform-in-direction remainder estimate or differentiability theorem is supplied. Existence of linear directional derivatives alone does not imply Frechet differentiability; hence neither D_y Phi nor its continuity follows from the preceding steps.",
