      "evidence": "The induction assumes derivatives through order k exist, then says “differentiating once more gives” an equation for order k+1 derivatives. This presupposes the very existence being proved. The cited linear-ODE lemma gives solutions for a fixed continuous time coefficient; it does not establish parameter differentiability or identify its solution as a new derivative. A difference-quotient or parameter-dependent linear-ODE argument is missing.",
